s=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Enemies have air and ground attributes.</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Lock on to ground enemies with the aim and destroy them with missiles.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Defeat airborne enemies with standard shots, power shots, or missiles fired from your ship.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>About Fanbit Forms and Weapons</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Fanbits are autonomous remote-controlled machines that deploy around your ship.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Fanbits can switch between attack and barrier forms.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Remaining energy Since the energy gauge is limited, when it reaches zero, it must be combined with your ship and recharged.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Weapon bags are dropped from supply ships, allowing you to select your Funbit's weapon by retrieving them.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Laser beam, shotgun, or circular orbital shot.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>About power packs</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >- Power packs are dropped by destroying certain enemy ships. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >By retrieving them, you can increase speed, extend your aim, extend your Funbit, replenish your shield, and more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game ends when your ship is hit and its shield level reaches zero.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >(There is no limit to the number of continues, so you can start the stage over again.)</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p>",
